---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy/' },
];

const lastUpdated = 'June 12, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Kashi Dwar (kashidwar.com)"
  description="Kashi Dwar's privacy policy — what data we do and don't collect, how cookies and third-party advertising (such as Google AdSense) may be used, and your choices."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <section class="texture-silk bg-indigo-night pt-10 pb-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} tone="dark" />
      <h1 class="font-display mt-8 text-4xl font-semibold text-cream sm:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-cream/60">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="texture-paper bg-cream py-12">
    <div class="prose-kashi mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <p>
        Kashi Dwar ("we", "this site", kashidwar.com) is a content website about Varanasi.
        We believe in collecting as little of your data as possible — ideally none. This page
        explains plainly what happens when you visit.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect directly: nothing</h2>
      <p>
        Kashi Dwar is a static website. We do not require accounts, do not have login forms,
        do not run our own analytics by default, and do not collect, store or sell personal
        information. If you email us, we see your email address and message and use them only
        to reply; we don't add you to any list.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The site itself does not set cookies for its own functionality. However, third-party
        services described below may set cookies when enabled. You can clear or block cookies
        in your browser settings at any time; the site will work fully without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense) — disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        We may display advertising served by <strong>Google AdSense</strong> or similar
        third-party networks to support the cost of running this site. When advertising is
        active:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies (such as the DoubleClick/Ad
          cookie) to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
        </li>
        <li>
          Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve
          personalised ads. You can opt out of personalised advertising at
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Ads Settings</a>,
          or via <a href="https://youradchoices.com" rel="noopener nofollow">youradchoices.com</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Visitors in the EEA/UK and other regions with consent requirements will be shown a
          consent mechanism before any advertising cookies are set, as required by law and by
          Google's EU User Consent Policy.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Ads are always visually distinguishable from our editorial content, and our
        recommendations are never paid placements.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If we add privacy-respecting analytics in future (to learn which guides help people
        most), we will prefer cookieless, aggregate tools and update this page before doing so.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links and embedded content</h2>
      <p>
        Our pages link to external sites (official temple portals, photographers' pages,
        booking resources). Once you leave kashidwar.com, those sites' own privacy policies
        apply. Fonts are currently loaded from Google Fonts, which may log requests as
        described in Google's privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a general-audience travel guide and does not knowingly collect any
        information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your jurisdiction (GDPR in the EU/UK, CCPA in California, DPDP Act in
        India), you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data. Since we hold
        none beyond any email you've sent us, exercising these rights is simple: write to us
        and we'll delete your correspondence on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We'll update this page whenever our practices change — for example, before enabling
        advertising or analytics — and revise the "last updated" date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:namaste@kashidwar.com">namaste@kashidwar.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
